# GitHub uses Linguist (https://github.com/github-linguist/linguist) for
# syntax highlighting. Linguist doesn't have a knot grammar, so we tell it
# to highlight .knot files as Python. The match is good: `#` comments,
# `def`/`if`/`else`/`for`/`while`/`return`/`in`/`not`/`and`/`or` are all
# keywords in both, and string/number literals line up. Braces just stay
# unstyled, which is acceptable.
#
# `linguist-detectable` opts the extension into language stats on GitHub.
*.knot         linguist-language=Python linguist-detectable=true
*.knot.annot   linguist-language=Text
